 "summary": "The monoid instance and iterate API are new material for `RootPairingIsogeny P P`; Mathlib's `Monoid (Hom P P)` / `Monoid (Equiv P P)` are on different types and have no `pow_*` or exponent-orbit lemmas. The `mul_*`/`one_*` restatements are the same pattern Mathlib uses (`Hom.weightMap_mul`, `Hom.weightMap_one`) and are needed since simp cannot unfold `Monoid.mul` to `comp`; the renamed `*_mul_self` theorems leave no compatibility aliases.",
